<title>SEYCHELLES: CHINESE PREMIER STARTS AFRICAN TOUR IN SEYCHELLES.</title>
<headline>CHINESE PREMIER STARTS AFRICAN TOUR IN SEYCHELLES.</headline>
<dateline>VICTORIA, Seychelles 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chinese Prime Minister Li Peng arrived in the Seychelles on Saturday at the start of a seven-nation African tour, officials said.</p>
<p>Li brought six of his ministers and a planeload of about 140 businessmen and journalists.</p>
<p>He will leave for the African mainland on Monday and will visit Zambia, Mozambique, Gabon, Cameroon, Nigeria and Tanzania until May 14.</p>
</text>
